<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ bills yields close higher in thin trade.</title>
<headline>NZ bills yields close higher in thin trade.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>---------------Snapshot at close-----------------</p>
<p>Figures in brackets compare against previous day's close</p>
<p>FUTURES					  PHYSICAL YIELD</p>
<p>90-DAY BILLS (MAR) 92.64  (PREV 62.68) 90-DAYS 7.87   (-0.02)</p>
<p>3-YR BONDS   (MAR) 93.00 (PREV 93.00)  02/00   7.03   (nil)</p>
<p>10-YR BONDS  (MAR) 92.77 (PREV 92.77)  11/06   7.25   (-0.03)</p>
<p>OVERNIGHT CASH 7.90 PCT (PREV 7.95)    US 5-YR  6.13 (PREV 6.13)</p>
<p>NZD/USD 0.7064/71 (PREV 0.7072/79)     US 10-YR 6.33 (PREV 6.33)</p>
<p>TWI 67.43 (PREV 67.28)		     US 30-YR 6.59 (PREV 6.58)</p>
<p>--------------------------(Dec 27)------------------------------</p>
<p>* Bank bill yields close a few points higher</p>
<p>* Volumes minimal</p>
<p>* Next focus inflation data due on January 17</p>
<p>New Zealand bank bill yields closed a couple of points higher on very light volumes on Friday.</p>
<p>Dealers said the market was exceedingly thin and they don't expect any pick-up until the New Year, possibly until inflation data comes out on January 17.</p>
